  <section id="codium">
    <h2>3. Cost and Vector Codium plans</h2>
    <p>
      Vector is free to download and use. Vector Codium is an optional monthly plan that gives you coding models
      through Vector without provider keys of your own, with the plan features listed for each plan at
      <a href="/codium">vectordev.ai/codium</a>. Services you connect through your own accounts, including model
      providers, external agents and hosting, may charge you separately under their own terms. Free models are subject
      to quotas, rate limits and availability; continued free access is not guaranteed.
    </p>
    <p>
      Before you pay, the checkout page shows the plan, its monthly price, any applicable taxes and the total payable.
      Stripe processes payments for Vector.
    </p>

    <h3 id="codium-plans">Monthly plans</h3>
    <p>
      Vector Codium is sold as monthly plans only. There are no top-ups and no overage charges: Vector never charges
      you for usage beyond your plan's price. Your plan renews automatically each month at the price shown at checkout
      until you cancel. You can cancel at any time in your account; cancelling stops future renewals, and you keep your
      plan until the end of the period you have paid for.
    </p>
    <p>
      An upgrade to a higher plan starts a new monthly period on the day you upgrade and is charged in full at the
      higher plan's price. The unused usage of your current month carries into that new period only, and ends at its
      renewal. A downgrade starts at your next renewal; until then you keep your current plan.
    </p>
    <p>
      If a payment fails, Vector Codium and your plan's features pause until the payment succeeds. A failed payment
      does not extend the month: the period still ends on its original date. If payment is still not made after
      Stripe's retries, your plan ends. A full refund of a payment, or a dispute of it, ends what that payment bought.
      If a payment is reported as possibly fraudulent, Vector may refund it and end the plan. Access is suspended while
      a payment is disputed or flagged as possibly fraudulent.
    </p>
    <p>
      New Max and Ultra subscriptions, including upgrades to them from Plus or Pro, start with reduced limits for a
      short period, such as fewer cloud computer hours or, if the first payment was not confirmed through your bank's
      authentication, less of the month's usage in the first days. The plan page describes these starting limits.
      Records of purchases are retained as required by law.
    </p>

    <h3 id="codium-models">Models and limits</h3>
    <p>
      Models, usage and limits differ by plan and are listed at <a href="/codium">vectordev.ai/codium</a>. A model may
      be temporarily unavailable, and Vector may replace a model with a comparable one. Vector does not
      reduce the usage, models or limits included in a month you have paid for. Changes to plan prices, or to the usage,
      models or limits a plan includes, will be communicated before they apply, with an opportunity to cancel and any
      consent required by law, and apply from your next renewal after the notice.
    </p>

    <h3 id="codium-usage">Usage</h3>
    <p>
      Your plan's usage is shown only as a whole-number percentage of the month, and Codium work is labelled
      “Codium” instead of with token counts or prices. The percentage may lag requests still being processed. Usage
      does not roll over: what is left when a period ends expires with it, and only an upgrade carries unused usage, as
      described above. Some plans also have a daily limit, a share of the month that can be used in one day (UTC).
      Usage is not a promise of a number of tokens, requests, completed tasks or successful results.
    </p>
    <p>
      How fast usage goes depends on the selected model, input and output, reasoning, conversation history, repeated
      repository context, tool use and the number of agents or model calls. Large tasks and parallel agents can use it
      quickly. Review usage and model selection in your account and supervise automated work. When the month's usage is
      used up, Vector Codium stops until your plan renews; when a day's share is used up on a plan with a daily limit,
      it stops until the next UTC day. Your own keys and free models keep working.
    </p>
    <p>
      To the extent permitted by law, accurately metered usage is not refundable solely because your usage ran out
      sooner than expected, an estimate differed from actual usage, or AI output did not complete your task. This does
      not excuse incorrect charges, duplicate billing or a failure to provide the plan you paid for. Contact us about
      suspected errors so we can investigate and correct confirmed billing errors. Any refund, cancellation, service
      guarantee or other consumer right required by applicable law continues to apply. Usage has no cash value and is
      not transferable, except where applicable law requires otherwise.
    </p>

    <h3 id="codium-coming">Items tagged “Coming”</h3>
    <p>
      Vector Velocity is in development and is not part of what any subscription buys today. If it launches, we intend
      to offer it only on Max and Ultra. We don't promise that it will launch, or when. The same applies to every item
      tagged “Coming” on Vector's pages: it is not part of what any subscription buys today, and we don't promise that
      it will launch, or when.
    </p>

    <h3 id="codium-github">GitHub agents on Codium</h3>
    <p>
      For runs of Vector's GitHub agent on your plan, Vector sells only Codium model access inside runs in your own
      repository, on your own Actions minutes. Runs execute under your GitHub account and GitHub's terms, and GitHub
      bills the Actions minutes they use. Runs may do only that repository's software work, such as fixing, reviewing,
      testing or maintaining its code. Anyone with write, maintain or admin access to a repository you connect to your
      plan can start runs that use your plan. Agent time is measured by Vector from Codium requests, not from GitHub's
      minutes. Vector's GitHub agent also works without a plan, with your own model key stored as a repository secret.
    </p>

    <div id="codium-hosted" data-where-available="computer overnight">
      <h3>Cloud computer (where available)</h3>
      <p>
        Where your plan includes a cloud computer that Vector runs for you, the time it runs counts toward your month's
        usage and toward your plan's cloud computer hours, including jobs you queue to run overnight. Vector may stop or
        pause a session, for example when it reaches its time limit, sits idle, or is used against these Terms. Do not
        use it for cryptocurrency mining, spam, scraping a website against that site's terms, solving CAPTCHAs or
        bypassing bot checks; Vector hands sign-in fields and CAPTCHAs to you. The browser profile is wiped after each
        job. The computer's disk is kept between jobs for the period your plan lists. After your plan ends, Vector tells
        you, keeps the disk for 14 days so you can download your files, and then deletes it.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div id="codium-ops" data-where-available="on-call release-guard ship-desk">
      <h3>Production checks (where available)</h3>
      <p>
        Where your plan includes On Call, Release Guard or Ship Desk, Vector checks only domains you have verified.
        Vector's GitHub App writes to a repository only where that repository opts in with a
        <code>.vector/ops.json</code> file, and then only to open pull requests automatically, such as one that reverts a
        release. Vector never merges a pull request; you decide whether to merge. On Call is Vector's agent, not a person.
        Vector makes no uptime, availability or response-time promise for your sites or for these checks, and a check or
        alert can be late or missed.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h3 id="codium-consent">Starting your plan, withdrawal and founding members</h3>
    <p>
      When you subscribe, you ask Vector to start your plan immediately. Where the law gives you a right to withdraw
      from the contract within 14 days, as in the European Union, you can still withdraw within 14 days of subscribing
      by contacting us, but you pay for what you used before you withdrew, and we refund the rest of that payment.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you subscribed as a founding member, your price won't go up while you stay subscribed. If you change plans, you
      pay the new plan's current price. Founding members on Plus and Pro also get 10% more usage; this does not apply to
      Max or Ultra. Founding membership ends when your subscription ends.
    </p>
  </section>

